# Hero section consistency

When editing any page hero (home, services listing, hire resources, or service detail), preserve this shared pattern. Do not invent a new hero structure per page.

## Required structure

1. Full-bleed background image (edge-to-edge), not an inset card or side panel
2. Dark overlay for text contrast — use **`bg-black/35`** on all marketing heroes (`Hero`, `ServiceHero`, `MobileServiceHero`) so the background image stays clearly visible (same visibility standard as home)
3. Centered content stack: optional orange uppercase badge → title → short subtitle → CTA group
4. Outfit / site `font-sans` only — no alternate display fonts in heroes
5. Prefer reusing `ServiceHero` / `MobileServiceHero` (with `backgroundImage`) or the home `Hero` component instead of one-off hero markup
6. Mobile development hero asset: `/images/mobile-development/hero-ai.png` (AI-generated atmospheric mobile/tech background)

## Overlay (shared with home)

- **All full-bleed page heroes** (home, services, mobile development, hire): `bg-black/35`
- Do **not** use `/40`, `/55`, `/58`, `/60`, or heavier overlays that hide the background image
- Keep home and mobile development at the **same** overlay strength so image visibility matches
- CTA / inset cards may use the same or lighter overlays (e.g. `bg-black/35`) — that is separate from full-page heroes

## No orange divider under the hero

- Do **not** place an orange gradient bar (`h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-600…`) on the first section directly below a hero
- Hero → next section should meet cleanly (optional subtle `border-border` only, no orange stripe)

## CTAs

- Primary: solid orange button (`bg-orange-600`), optional trailing arrow
- Secondary (when present): outline on dark (`border-white/70`, transparent fill, white text)
- Services-style pages: pair **primary action** + **Learn More** (or equivalent secondary)
- Hire Resources: **Hire Now** (primary → contact) + **Learn More** (secondary → roles / hire page)

## Do not

- Replace full-bleed heroes with gradient-only or card-inset heroes without an explicit request
- Add floating badges, stat chips, or promo stickers over hero media
- Crowd the first viewport with extra sections (stats, schedules, multiple copy blocks)
- Darken the overlay so the background image disappears, or lighten so white text fails contrast

## Performance

- Hero images: use Next.js `Image` with `fill`, `priority` on LCP heroes, and compressed assets (prefer WebP / reasonable `quality` when available)
- Keep secondary section backgrounds lightweight (compressed WebP, no huge PNGs)
